-"Lines to voice" counts every changed line plus each new narrator line (m02 and m03 voice their narration, so m02's new narrator line needs a clip; m04 to m07 have no audio yet). A delivery note is part of the line's cache key, so a tagged line needs a new clip even where its words were already voiced. Voltage's `m04_npc_voltage.ink:507` is a sequence, so its one line is two clips. No audio was generated and no clip was deleted; the 43 old clips (34 in m02, 9 in m03) are now orphans for `tts:wasted` to list once the new lines are voiced.
