 ## Checks
 
 For each mission: `scripts/compile-ink.sh <mission>` (no failures), `dialoguelint.mjs` totals identical to before the change (and no `inline-direction` warning with the voice-tag branch's lint), and the validator (`--no-graph`) run on the old and new ink with an identical list of errors and warnings.
 
+## Merging and audio
+
+Merge `build/voice-direction-tag` first, then this branch. Merged the other way round, every tagged line runs through the default branch of `processGameActionTags` (`chat-helpers.js`) and logs "Unknown game action tag: delivery": harmless, but noisy.
+
+Taking a cue out changes the line's text, so the 43 m02 and m03 lines with a committed clip lose it the moment this branch merges, whichever branch goes first. A server that cannot generate audio plays them silent; one that can generates each live on first play. Before deploying, run `tts:batch_generate` for m02 and m03 (the clips it makes carry the notes), then `tts:wasted` for the orphans. m04 to m07 have no audio and are unaffected.
+
